\details{
Internal coded scale profile helpers

Developer documentation for the scalar coded scale profile interval and
its wrappers.

If \code{T_D(d)} is the full criterion profiled subject to coded contrast \code{d},
then
\code{set(d: T_D(d) <= c) = set(Delta(zeta): W(zeta) <= c)}.
\code{delta_profile_interval.optimize()} evaluates this range with the same
method specific reductions used for projection, but with the
\code{chisq(df = 1)} cutoff. It does not construct a separate target grid or run
an optimizer over a coded equality constraint.

For \code{splrt}, this profile statistic and interval are exactly the ordinary
two sample empirical likelihood statistic and interval for the numerically
coded observations. For \code{lrt}, the analytic mean ellipsoid reduction leaves
only the deterministic radial search over the two arm logits.

\code{augmentDeltaInference()} adds only the point estimate. Confidence
intervals are computed on demand by \code{\link[=confint.trunc_comp_fit]{confint.trunc_comp_fit()}}.
}
